<title>NEW ZEALAND: HongkongBank cuts NZ floating mortgage rate.</title>
<headline>HongkongBank cuts NZ floating mortgage rate.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>HongkongBank on Thursday said it had cut its New Zealand floating mortgage rate to 8.95 percent from 9.60 percent, effective immediately for new business and from May 1 for existing customers.</p>
<p>The move follows other cuts by mainstream banks, who have acted in response to lower-than-expected inflation data for the March quarter.</p>
<p>HongkongBank targets high net worth individuals.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
